%N A400442 Numbers k such that the trajectory of k->ord(10,k) reaches 1 before reaching a number not coprime to 10. Here ord(b,k) is the multiplicative order of b modulo k.
%C A400442 Closed under multiplication; see A400096 for details.
%H A400442 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400442/b400442.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..3902</a> (all terms <= 10^10)
%e A400442 Powers of 3 are terms: 3^n -> 3^(n-2) -> 3^(n-4) -> ... -> 3 or 1.
%e A400442 757 is a term: 757 -> 27 -> 3 -> 1.
%e A400442 440334654777631 is a term: 440334654777631 -> 27 -> 3 -> 1.
%t A400442 (* okQ is defined at A400096 *)
%t A400442 Select[Range[40000], okQ[#, 10] &] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 26 2026 *)
%o A400442 (PARI) isok(n, 10) \\ see A400096 for isok
%Y A400442 See A400096 for list of sequences in other bases.
